<main class="wrap">
 <a class="back" href="/projects">← All projects</a>
 <div class="meta m"><span style="color:var(--ink)">Build 04</span><span class="ln"></span><span>Job discovery &amp; application orchestration</span><span class="ln"></span><span><span class="rec"></span>Used on 100+ real application workflows</span></div>

 <section class="top">
  <div>
   <h1 style="font-size:clamp(76px,11.5vw,176px)">Job Beast</h1>
   <div class="kick">The job description can change what I emphasize. <span>It can never change what's true.</span></div>
   <p class="lede">Not an auto-apply bot. A system that treats job searching like real software: it watches many sources, ranks roles by fit and timing, rules out what I can't take, builds the strongest <b style="font-weight:500">truthful</b> résumé my evidence supports, and stops to ask whenever a decision is mine.</p>
   <div class="acts"><a class="pillb solid" href="#pipe">Walk the pipeline <span class="arr"></span></a><a class="pillb" href="#truth">The no-lying rule</a><a class="pillb" href="https://github.com/VishalkiranRaichur/VishalJobBeast">Source</a></div>
  </div>
  <div class="facts rv">
   <div><span>Role</span><span>Solo · built for my own search</span></div>
   <div><span>Real use</span><span>100+ application workflows</span></div>
   <div><span>Sources</span><span>Simplify · LinkedIn · JobSpy</span></div>
   <div><span>Safety</span><span>Human-in-the-loop by design</span></div>
   <div><span>Stack</span><span>Python · SQLite · LaTeX · Playwright</span></div>
  </div>
 </section>

 <!-- 01 PROBLEM -->
 <section class="sec">
  <div class="sl m"><span><span class="n">01</span> · The problem</span><span>Why it's a systems problem</span></div>
  <div class="sh"><h2 class="rv">Job searching is a messy distributed system.</h2><p class="rv d1">Thousands of postings, many sources, deadlines that vanish and rules hidden in the fine print. <b>I wanted to stop treating it like a chore and build it like a real system.</b></p></div>
  <div class="pains">
   <div class="pn rv"><b>∞</b><h5>Too many sources</h5><p>No single board shows every opening.</p></div>
   <div class="pn rv d1"><b>×3</b><h5>Same job, again</h5><p>One role shows up on LinkedIn, Simplify and the employer's own site.</p></div>
   <div class="pn rv d2"><b>⏱</b><h5>Gone fast</h5><p>Strong roles fill up early, so timing matters.</p></div>
   <div class="pn rv"><b>¶</b><h5>Buried rules</h5><p>Eligibility hides deep in the posting.</p></div>
   <div class="pn rv d1"><b>≠</b><h5>Tailor, don't lie</h5><p>Every application needs tailoring without inventing anything.</p></div>
  </div>
 </section>

 <!-- 02 PIPELINE -->
 <section class="sec" id="pipe">
  <div class="sl m"><span><span class="n">02</span> · The pipeline</span><span>Click each stage</span></div>
  <div class="sh"><h2 class="rv">Nine stages. Each one exists because something broke.</h2><p class="rv d1">Most of these design decisions came from real failures. <b>Instead of patching one job, I fixed the whole class of failure</b> in the system.</p></div>
  <div class="pipe rv">
   <div class="plist" id="plist"></div>
   <div class="pdet" id="pdet"></div>
  </div>
 </section>

 <!-- 03 TRUTH -->
 <section class="sec" id="truth">
  <div class="sl m"><span><span class="n">03</span> · The soul of the project</span><span>Evidence grounding</span></div>
  <div class="sh"><h2 class="rv">Tailor aggressively. Never hallucinate.</h2><p class="rv d1">Those two goals pull in opposite directions. So every experience, project, skill and metric lives in an <b>evidence bank with a stable ID</b>, and every résumé line has to trace back to one. A requirement with no evidence stays a gap.</p></div>
  <div class="ev rv">
   <div><div class="m">The job asks for</div>
    <div class="req"><span>Python</span><span class="k ex">EXACT</span><span class="id">SKILL-python · PROJ-orion</span></div>
    <div class="req"><span>SQL databases</span><span class="k ex">EXACT</span><span class="id">SKILL-sql · PROJ-forgedb</span></div>
    <div class="req"><span>Cloud infrastructure</span><span class="k um">UMBRELLA</span><span class="id">PROJ-pulsegrid (Docker workers)</span></div>
    <div class="req"><span>REST APIs</span><span class="k ad">ADJACENT</span><span class="id">EXP-rcc (Flask backend)</span></div>
    <div class="req"><span>C++</span><span class="k un">UNSUPPORTED</span><span class="id gap">no evidence → stays a gap</span></div>
    <p style="font-size:13.5px;color:var(--mut);margin-top:14px;font-family:PM;letter-spacing:.04em">ILLUSTRATIVE EXAMPLE · MATCH CLASSES ARE REAL</p></div>
   <div><div class="m">What the résumé gets</div>
    <div class="res"><div class="nm">Skills · Projects</div>
     <div class="ln"><span>Python, SQL, Docker, Flask</span><small>SKILL-*</small></div>
     <div class="ln"><span>Built an AI analyst that traces every figure to a source</span><small>PROJ-orion</small></div>
     <div class="ln"><span>Built a database engine with a B+ tree index</span><small>PROJ-forgedb</small></div>
     <div class="ln"><span>Built a backend for a local-AI readability app</span><small>EXP-rcc</small></div></div>
    <div class="gaprep">COVERAGE REPORT · C++ → UNSUPPORTED · reported, not added</div></div>
  </div>
 </section>

 <!-- 04 RANKING -->
 <section class="sec">
  <div class="sl m"><span><span class="n">04</span> · A ranking trade-off</span><span>Fit vs. freshness</span></div>
  <div class="sh"><h2 class="rv">New isn't the same as good.</h2><p class="rv d1">Sorting by posting time is a trap: a weak match posted five minutes ago would beat a great one from yesterday. So <b>fit and freshness are separate signals</b>, and freshness can help but never dominate.</p></div>
  <div class="rank rv">
   <div><div class="m">Queue priority = fit + freshness bonus</div>
    <div class="sw" id="sw"><button class="on" data-m="time">Sort by newest</button><button data-m="beast">Job Beast ranking</button></div>
    <div id="jobs"></div>
    <p style="font-family:PM;font-size:10.5px;color:var(--mut);margin-top:16px;letter-spacing:.06em">ILLUSTRATIVE JOBS · REAL RULES</p></div>
   <div class="rules2"><div class="m" style="padding:0 0 10px;border:0;display:block">The rules</div>
    <div><span>01</span><p>Freshness is a <b>bounded bonus, at most +15</b>, decaying across age bands.</p></div>
    <div><span>02</span><p>No bonus at all <b>below a minimum fit score</b>.</p></div>
    <div><span>03</span><p><b>Fast lane</b> only when a role is both ≤3 hours old and fit ≥70.</p></div>
    <div><span>04</span><p>Stale fast-lane entries are demoted on every re-rank.</p></div>
    <div class="bands" style="border:0;padding:0"><div style="height:100%"><small>1H</small></div><div style="height:78%"><small>3H</small></div><div style="height:55%"><small>6H</small></div><div style="height:34%"><small>12H</small></div><div style="height:16%"><small>24H</small></div></div>
    <p style="font-family:PM;font-size:10px;color:var(--mut);margin-top:30px;border:0;padding:0">BONUS DECAY SHAPE · ILLUSTRATIVE</p></div>
  </div>
 </section>

 <!-- 05 STATE -->
 <section class="sec">
  <div class="sl m"><span><span class="n">05</span> · State management</span><span>What happens after something goes wrong</span></div>
  <div class="sh"><h2 class="rv">Failures aren't exceptions. They're states.</h2><p class="rv d1">Every job lives in a persisted state machine. The radar re-ranks constantly, so it has to know <b>which jobs it may never touch again</b>, and a broken posting only fails itself, never the batch.</p></div>
  <div class="sm rv">
   <svg viewBox="0 0 1180 330">
    <g font-family="PM" font-size="10" letter-spacing="1.2" fill="#6f6d68"><text x="20" y="20">DISCOVER</text><text x="300" y="20">PREPARE</text><text x="600" y="20">EXECUTE</text><text x="900" y="20">OUTCOME</text></g>
    <g stroke="#111" stroke-opacity=".12"><path d="M280 10V320M580 10V320M880 10V320"/></g>
    <g font-family="PM" font-size="11" text-anchor="middle">
     <rect x="40" y="60" width="200" height="40" fill="#fff" stroke="#111"/><text x="140" y="85">QUEUED</text>
     <rect x="40" y="150" width="200" height="40" fill="#fff" stroke="#111" stroke-dasharray="4 4"/><text x="140" y="175">NEEDS_HYDRATION</text>
     <rect x="320" y="60" width="220" height="40" fill="#fff" stroke="#111"/><text x="430" y="85">READY_FOR_OPERATOR</text>
     <rect x="320" y="150" width="220" height="40" fill="#fff" stroke="#111" stroke-dasharray="4 4"/><text x="430" y="175">NEEDS CONFIRMATION</text>
     <rect x="320" y="240" width="220" height="40" fill="#f6f2ea" stroke="#111"/><text x="430" y="265">INELIGIBLE</text>
